35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Good morning. The winter closures didn’t stop the halls, and outreach attendance was surprisingly strong. That gives me hope for steady access.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The bus cuts are severe. Yet remote use peaks after nine, when we lock up. That mismatch worries me deeply.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Shizue, wait! The old outreach sheets show forty people showed up! And the evening groups from six years ago still meet! We have proof it works!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The grant covers sessions for a year, then the flat budget absorbs them. Meanwhile, vehicle costs overran by a third. That’s a structural trap, not a temporary blip.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, those unaided groups prove a gap. My register shows no staff trained to supervise outside facilitators. We cannot assume skills exist.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, I hear your caution. But those halls kept their own timetables despite the closures. That suggests the community can sustain these services independently, without relying on our fragile logistics.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that independence is fragile. If we lock at nine, we miss the peak remote users. We must align hours with actual demand.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, but the groups ran without us for six years! That proves the community handles it. We just need to stop ignoring the old records!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, six years of luck isn’t a strategy. The grant expires, the flat budget absorbs the cost, and the vehicle overruns eat the rest. It’s a slow bleed.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the funding trap is real, but my data shows a skills deficit. We lack supervisors for outside facilitators. We cannot expand without training staff first.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, I understand the financial worry. But if the community sustains these services independently, we might avoid the very logistics that caused those overruns.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the financial risk is real, but the access gap is immediate. We cannot ignore the people stranded by the bus cuts.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, but the records prove it works! Why do we keep guessing when the old sheets show forty people showed up?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, forty attendees don’t pay for fuel. The grant is a one-year loan, not a gift. We need a model that survives the second year, not just the first.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, attendance proves demand, not capability. My register confirms no staff are trained to supervise outside facilitators. We must address this skills gap before expanding.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, I appreciate your caution. Perhaps we can pair the community’s independence with a small, focused training pilot to bridge that gap gently.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I agree. But please consider extending hours first. The remote peak is now, not later.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, the groups ran themselves for six years! That’s proof they don’t need us. Why are we ignoring the records that show it works?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, training is vital, but it’s a line item, not a strategy. We need a funding model that doesn’t evaporate when the grant expires.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, self-sustaining groups still require oversight. My data shows no staff trained to supervise outside facilitators. We must verify skills before adding duties.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
