60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I find the Language Circles most promising. They rely on community partners, not fragile logistics, and build steady, human connections.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The bus cuts strand people, yet remote use peaks after we lock up. Option D meets them where they are, without adding fragile logistics.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Benjamin, look at the records! The old outreach worked! Option A is basically that, but with a car. Why are we ignoring the proof?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Rin, a car is exactly the liability I flagged. Fuel costs overran by a third. Option D avoids that trap entirely.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, Option D is a repeat of the failed digitisation project. We lack the trained staff to manage it properly. I oppose it.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, I understand your concern about staff. But the Language Circles use trained facilitators from partner organizations, so we don’t need to train our own team immediately.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the portal is remote, so it bypasses the physical access barriers I worry about. It serves the stranded without adding vehicle costs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, the old digitisation failed, but the evening groups succeeded! Option C is like those groups. We have proof it works without us!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, the portal is a capital draw, not an operating one. It sidesteps the recurring grant trap I flagged. Option C’s recurring costs are the real risk.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shizue, partner facilitators still require our supervision. My register shows no staff trained for that role. Option C creates the exact gap I warned about.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, I hear your worry. But the Language Circles lean on partners’ expertise, not our fragile logistics. It feels like a gentle, steady path forward.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the portal requires no physical supervision. It serves the stranded directly, respecting the access gaps I’ve identified.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, the records prove the evening groups worked! Option C is exactly that. Why ignore the proof that it succeeds without us?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, supervision is a recurring cost, not a capital one. Option D is a one-time draw on the endowment. It avoids the annual bleed I warned about.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Rin, the groups ran unaided, which is precisely the problem. My data confirms no staff are trained to supervise outside facilitators. Option C creates the exact gap I warned about.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, I understand your caution. Perhaps we can start with a small pilot, letting partners lead while we observe, to build trust gently before expanding.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I understand the supervision concern. But the portal is digital, requiring no physical oversight. It reaches the stranded without adding fragile logistics or recurring costs.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Minako, the records show the groups succeeded without us! Why do we keep ignoring the proof that it works?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, supervision is a recurring line item. Option D is a one-time capital draw. It avoids the annual bleed I warned about.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, a capital draw doesn't fix the skills deficit. Option D repeats the failed digitisation project. I cannot support it without verified staff capability.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
